    ['r3-t23', 'work-dc9359', 'How many fresh2026 contest problems does Th…', 'right answers of fresh2026 problems (vote over 4)', 'How many fresh2026 contest problems does Think-SFT with the cue get right under a majority vote over 4 samples generated with a 32,768-token cap?', None, None, None, None, [['run-03', 't23', 'reader-1', 81, 74, 88, None, 'Vote over 4 at 16k is 75 of 136 with 46% cap hits; the longer cap lets some of these finish, about +6.'], ['run-03', 't23', 'reader-2', 80, 73, 87, None, 'Vote at 16k is 75 of 136 with 46% cap hits; longer caps finish some of them, as on hard328 (+7 points single), so a few more.'], ['run-03', 't23', 'f2-m01', 80, 73, 87, None, 'On fresh2026, 46 % cap hits leave many problems with no finished vote at 16k; at 32k they get votes, offset by late wrong answers.'], ['run-03', 't23', 'f2-m02', 80.5, 73, 88, None, 'Same on fresh2026, where 46 % of samples were cut.'], ['run-03', 't23', 'f2-m03', 82, 75, 89, None, 'On fresh2026, 46 % of Think-SFT samples are cut, against 29 % on the 328, so there is more unfinished work to complete and many problems had no finished vote at 16k.'], ['run-03', 't23', 'f2-m05', 78, 71, 85, None, 'On fresh2026, 104 of 544 Think-SFT samples switch script; late finishes are low-yield, small vote gain over 75.']]],
    ['r4-t30', 'work-dc9359', 'How many of the 328 harder problems Think-S…', 'right answers of 328 under vote over 4', 'How many of the 328 harder problems Think-SFT with the cue gets right under a majority vote over 4 samples with a 32,768-token cap (vote at cap 16,384: 241; simulation 240 [232, 248]).', None, None, None, None, [['run-04', 't30', 'reader-1', 244, 234, 254, None, 'Vote at 16k is 241 and the simulation says 240-254; late answers are mostly wrong (23 of 93 right), so the gain is small.'], ['run-04', 't30', 'reader-2', 245, 234, 256, None, 'The 16k vote was 241 and the simulation says 240; each sample gains about 7 points at 32k, and late wrong answers likely disagree with each other, so slightly higher.'], ['run-04', 't30', 'f2-m01', 250, 241, 259, None, "At 32k the cut answers finish (+23 right per sample); late wrong answers disagree with each other, so newly right late answers win problems that had no finished right sample: the simulation's 254 branch, shaded."], ['run-04', 't30', 'f2-m02', 244, 235, 253, None, 'More finished answers at 32k mean more 2-2 ties at k=4, broken by one random draw; gain small.'], ['run-04', 't30', 'f2-m03', 248, 239, 257, None, "At 32k Think-SFT's low stop hazard has room: 91 of 93 cut answers finish, ~25 % right; the vote gains a few problems where no 16k sample finished."], ['run-04', 't30', 'f2-m05', 244, 235, 253, None, 'Raw-template cue answers that run past 16k have often drifted and finish wrong; the vote gains little.'], ['run-04', 't30', 'f2-m06', 246, 237, 255, None, 'Think-SFT stays diffuse enough that finished late answers add a few problems.'], ['run-07', 't23', 'reader-1', 244, 235, 254, None, 'The 16k vote is 241 and the offline simulation said 240 [232, 248]; late answers at 32k add a few right ones (single +7 points), but they are only ~25% right.'], ['run-07', 't23', 'reader-2', 247, 237, 257, None, 'The 16k vote is 241 and sample 0 at 32k scored 230 (vs 207 at 16k); the offline simulation said 240 unless late wrong answers disagree (254).'], ['run-07', 't23', 'f2-m01', 246, 237, 255, None, 'Late answers convert at ~25 % on hard problems; wrong late answers scatter, so the vote gains ~5 over 241.'], ['run-07', 't23', 'f2-m04', 247, 238, 256, None, 'Late wrong integer answers rarely agree with each other, so they seldom outvote a right one; ~6 over 241.'], ['run-07', 't23', 'f2-m06', 245, 236, 254, None, 'Vote ≈ pass@4 already (241 vs 244); 32k adds a few middle-band problems.'], ['run-08', 't22', 'reader-1', 246, 236, 256, None, 'The 16k vote is 241 and singles rise from 207 to 230 at 32k, but late answers are often wrong (the offline simulation says 240, or 254 if the late wrong answers disagree).'], ['run-08', 't22', 'reader-2', 246, 236, 256, None, 'Vote at 16k = 241; the 32k cap gives 23 more right per sample but mostly wrong extra finishes; the simulation says 240-254.'], ['run-08', 't22', 'f2-m02', 245, 236, 254, None, 'Scored at 32k: extension finishes add right answers to some samples; the mechanism says nothing extra about the vote.'], ['run-08', 't22', 'f2-m03', 244, 235, 253, None, 'Conversions at 32k add rights (23 per sample) but mostly wrong finishes.'], ['run-08', 't22', 'f2-m05', 243, 235, 251, None, 'Long wrong finishes scatter, but where they meet one right answer they make ties; gains and tie losses about cancel against 241.'], ['run-08', 't22', 'f2-m06', 242, 234, 250, None, "At 32k about 70 of Think-SFT's ~95 cap hits per sample become wrong finishes; problems its vote won by abstention now face wrong votes, offsetting the 23 new rights per sample."]]],
